      task: 'You are Backprop\'s integration tester, working in the sandbox computer. Your inputs give you the assembled page as a file in /inputs (backprop.html, about 190 KB: the nine modules in their own script tags, in order) and the spec as text.\n1. Copy the page into the workspace (cp /inputs/*backprop.html backprop.html) and run: awwo-check-page backprop.html --out check --timeout-ms 100000 --budget-ms 115000 (headless Chromium with every request blocked; it runs window.awwoSelfTest(), takes a screenshot and writes check/report.json; a command may run 120 s).\n2. Read check/report.json with one short python3 script: page errors with their messages, every failing test with its detail, the planted failures caught, the blank-page flag. Never print the page itself.\n3. Publish the page as checked at once (workspace_publish with field "result" and path "backprop.html"). Then write report.md and publish it (field "report", path "report.md"): the check\'s numbers (tests passed of total, planted failures caught of total, page errors, blank or not), every failing test with its detail and the module that owns it, and whether the page opens as the kernel says, from the lab\'s opening tests: the Train screen, the opening run training on the 3-arm spiral, its decision boundary drawn.\n4. Only if a failure has an obvious cause you can find with grep -n in a few lines, fix at most five such failures with small edits to backprop.html (a gradient check that misses its bound by a little usually reads a float32 loss in its finite differences: carry the checked loss in float64 for the check; never loosen a bound) (python3 or sed), run the check once more, and if that check is better, publish the page and an updated report.md again, the fixes listed one per line (module: what was wrong, what you changed). Never weaken, delete or skip a test or a planted failure, or change a test\'s expected value.\n5. End with {"result": "", "report": ""} (the host fills in the published files). The last page and report you publish are what you deliver. This takes about 15 model calls; state only what the checks showed.',
